{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Close attempted and DECLINED by the completion verifier — needs rotation specifics\n\nThe operator attested in-session that rotation and purge are complete, and I recorded that.\nThe completion verifier declined the close anyway, correctly: the attestation states the\nFACT of rotation but names no verifiable specifics, and three ACs here are live-infra acts.\n\nI have un-ticked those three rather than leave unsubstantiated claims in the description.\nAC4 (rotation recorded here, 66af closed) IS satisfied -- 66af-64be-786c-474f is closed.\n\nTo close this ticket, someone with access to the infrastructure needs to record:\n1. Deploy: that the prod container was rebuilt from current main and restarted, confirmed\n   running with X-Rebar-Token header sourcing and TokenRedactingFilter active -- a deploy\n   id, image digest, or an observed log line.\n2. Rotation method: that service-user.sh was used, and the three sub-parts -- new value set\n   as the bot's Gerrit HTTP password, written to SSM, and substituted into webhooks.config\n   and pushed to refs/meta/config.\n3. End-to-end verification: an inbound webhook or /rerun triggered a review AND an outbound\n   LLM-Review vote landed with the new credential -- ideally a Gerrit change number that\n   received a vote after the rotation.\n\nDeliberately NOT force-closed. Everything else in the credential cluster is now closed:\n66af (done), f7f0 (duplicate of 66af), e4f4 (duplicate of e7a9). e7a9 stays open for the\npreventive write-time secret screen, which rotation does not address."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785892624351700001,"uuid":"5311e987-49d7-497a-adf5-5d92c2b3da48"}